# infokobuleti.com — project rules

## Product
All-in-one portal for Kobuleti (Adjara, Georgia): hotels & guesthouses, real estate (sale / rent / daily rent),
classifieds, job vacancies, city guide (beaches, sights, nature), news & events, useful info.
Audience: tourists, locals, property buyers and investors, job seekers, local businesses.

## Stack (do not change without asking me)
Laravel 13, PHP 8.4, PostgreSQL 17 + pgvector, Redis, Horizon, Scout + Meilisearch,
Blade + Livewire 4 + Alpine.js + Tailwind CSS v4 (Vite), Filament v5 admin at /admin,
Socialite (Google), spatie: permission, medialibrary, translatable, activitylog, backup, sitemap.
Laravel AI SDK (Anthropic provider), Reverb (real-time), Pest (tests), Laravel Boost (MCP).

## Server
Hostinger VPS, Ubuntu 24.04, Nginx, PHP-FPM. Project path: /var/www/infokobuleti.
Staging: dev.infokobuleti.com (basic auth + noindex). Production: infokobuleti.com (from Phase 11).
Never run destructive commands (migrate:fresh, db:wipe, DROP, rm -rf, force pushes) without asking me first.
Never commit .env or secrets.

## Design source of truth
- design-reference/Homepage.dc.html: finished homepage. Reuse its markup, spacing, cards, buttons, hover effects.
- design-reference/DESIGN-PROMPT.md: full style spec. design-reference/MEMORY.md: design decisions.
- Every new page must look like the same product. Pages without a design are composed from existing
  components; never invent new colors, fonts, radii or shadows.

## Design tokens
navy #0a1a2f (header, footer, headings, rating chips, sale/rent badges, active filters), navy-hover #1b304d,
text-secondary #3a4a5f, line #e8edf3, line-strong #c9d3df, surface-alt #f5f7fa, white #ffffff.
coral #d4602a = the ONLY action accent (primary buttons, CTA, search button, hover fills, hearts, "ახალი" badge),
coral-hover #e06d36, coral-pressed #bf5323, price text #b44f1e, coral-tint #fcece2.
sea #2f6f9f only for sea temperature. Hero search tab hues only: hotels #2f6f9f, real estate #2e7d6b,
classifieds #b5622f, jobs #6a4f9e. No other bright colors; no gradients except the hero overlay.
Fonts: Noto Sans Georgian (UI/body 400-700), Noto Serif Georgian (headings 600), Outfit (logo only, 300/700).
Radius: cards 16px, buttons 12px, pills 999px.
Card hover: translateY(-4px) + shadow 0 20px 40px -16px rgba(10,26,47,.22); image zoom 1.05 over .7s.
Sections fade up 24px on scroll (0.8s). Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
Icons: one line icon set only, 1.5px stroke, rounded caps. No emoji, no filled icons (except saved heart).
Breakpoints: >=1240 full nav, <1100 tablet, <720 mobile. Touch targets >= 44px.

## Language and locale
- UI default Georgian (ka), plus en and ru. URLs: / (ka), /en/..., /ru/...
- Every UI string goes through lang files (lang/ka, lang/en, lang/ru). Never hardcode Georgian text in Blade or PHP.
- User content is translatable (jsonb columns).
- Phone: +995 5XX XX XX XX. Currency: GEL (₾) default; USD/EUR via National Bank of Georgia rates.
- Timezone Asia/Tbilisi. Georgian date formats.
- Code, comments and commit messages in English.

## Code conventions
- Thin controllers. Business logic in app/Actions and app/Services. Form Requests for validation,
  Policies for authorization, PHP backed Enums for statuses and types (labels from lang files).
- Shared listing behavior via traits/interfaces: HasStatus, HasSlug, HasLocation, Favoritable, Reviewable,
  Promotable, Reportable, InteractsWithMedia.
- No N+1: Model::preventLazyLoading() outside production. Index all foreign keys and filter columns.
- Every external service (SMS, payments, AI, weather, currency, maps) sits behind an interface
  with a fake driver for local and tests.
- Queue anything slow: images, SMS, email, AI, search indexing.
- Pest tests for every feature. Before finishing a task run: php artisan test, ./vendor/bin/pint,
  ./vendor/bin/phpstan analyse.

## Workflow
- Use Laravel Boost MCP tools to check docs and package versions before writing code.
- If a requirement is unclear or risky, ask me before implementing.
- At the end of each phase: run all checks, commit "Phase N: <summary>", push, then report:
  what was built, how I verify it in the browser, what I must do manually (keys, DNS, accounts),
  known gaps.

